        "title": "Learning Hindu Culture",
        "text": "Our first full day in Kathmandu, we visited this temple and it was a great way to learn how the people of Nepal live their lives around what happens with the temple and their gods. I liked being able to see how they ritually went through the cremation of the dead and how each person handled it. \nThis temple received some damage from the earthquake but not as much as other places. \nHowever, I did not like that there were locals every where in the temple who had set up little places to sell things and were constantly going up to tourists trying to sell their items. It just didn't seem very sacred to me. But it could just be how their culture operates. ",
