        "title": "Holiest place to visit in Nepal, alas only Hindus allowed",
        "text": "This is the most holiest site in Nepal. This was the place where lord Shiva took incarnation of an animal (all that anyways you can wiki around). This temple only allows Hindus to visit, don't understand why the restriction. It is very peaceful inside and really beautiful, the roof was made of gold they say now not sure but surely the color is golden still :). Apart from the main temple there are many other temples also and you can also directly go to the Bagmati river from the temple itself. Non-hindus are allowed to visit temples on the other side of Bagmati you can see Pashupati standing in all her/his glory. Should go there at least once if you are in Kathmandu.",
