        "title": "Great but watch out for some things!",
        "text": "this Temple was really great to explore! it was fun because they also had all the wild life. Heres a few tips for non local travelers\n1.) beware the monkeys! :they are not nice and will steal things;clothes, snacks and gagets\n2.) fake religios people : we went with locals who knew all the ins and out and there would be people at the temples who pretended to be things they weren't. they would dress up in very cool traditional (looking) outfits and offer pictures but then would want money. it is a scam .\n3.) cremations :being a temple they do have real ceremonies and such there including funerals where they would burn the body's in the open then dust the ash off into the river. so watch out for smokey areas cause your probably breathing burnt flesh and to be respectful and not intrude / take pictures of these events because it is someones family member.\n\nbut its truly amazing to experience this place the list off good is just way to long to rite out :)",
